*Infinite [[Vlad de Sable]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Skelecat (Enemy)|Skelecats]] spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zollow]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 36.67~43.33 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,300f</sup>.
*1 [[Lord Gravey]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*2 [[Gobble]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Miss Haka]] spawns as the boss after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
[[Gold Brick Cat (Special Cat)|King Nekokhamen]] is decent here with [[Immune to Toxic]] and Resistant versus Floating, although he is quite expensive to get and not very practical to use outside his designated counters. A better meatshield option here would be [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong]], who will deal with the main Zombie threats, but he will die easily if hit by the Zollows' or Gobbles' toxic. Use backliners to deal with Lord Gravey. Once he is dead, you should not have too much trouble.

Be sure to exploit Miss Haka's multiple knockbacks to keep her away from your base using any of the following: rushers, [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]], [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] and the Holy Blast cannon. Always have something ready in case Miss Haka reaches your base because she will only need a few hits to destroy it.

